# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Manages exactly `ddns.general.enabled`, `manual_config`, `server_ip` and
`server_port` on **stable OPNsense 26.7.7 or newer** with the compatible scalar
model. The singleton already exists; create applies explicit desired settings
over an authoritative appliance baseline, not a new object or a default reset.
Use only one Terraform owner for these fields.

Credentials require read permission for `/api/core/firmware/status` and
`/api/kea/ddns/get`, write permission for `/api/kea/ddns/set`, and permission for
`/api/kea/service/reconfigure`. Grant these using the appliance API permission
selector. Product identity, stable version and the actual four-field DDNS model
are verified before mutation; no generic-option catalog is required.

`enabled` is required to make service-state intent explicit. Omitted optional
fields preserve appliance, imported and prior values, including at creation and
after removing an argument. API defaults are observed, never imposed. Explicit
`false` is written. Unknown configured values remain unknown and must resolve
before a write; they are not replaced by prior values or defaults. Only explicitly
configured arguments are sent in targeted partial writes.

`server_ip` accepts canonical IPv4 or the exact upstream `any` sentinel, not
empty strings, IPv6, CIDR or lists. `server_port` is an integer from 1 through
65535; zero/empty does not clear. `manual_config` owns the flag only, not manual
configuration files, hooks or integrations. DHCPv4/6 settings, Control Agent,
generic options and parent links are outside this owner's scope. Kea reconfigure
is shared; it does not imply only one process reloads or prove DNS delivery.

